' F13 -- Professor batch review of AI-extracted content.
' Chapter 5 (Implementation). UML activity diagram.
' Claim supported: the human-in-the-loop step is CORRECTIVE, not GATING.
' AI-extracted content is student-visible from the moment the parse finishes;
' "Done reviewing" is a localStorage flag, not a publish action.
@startuml f13-batch-review
!include _style.iuml

title Batch review — corrective, not gating

|#F2F2F2|Professor|
start
:upload N files at /professor/upload;

|#DCDCDC|Pipeline (per file)|
:one parse_runs row per file,\nsharing a batch_id;
:parse, synthesise, persist\nlectures + slides + quiz_questions;
:**lecture is LIVE in its course**\n**the moment the job finishes**;
note right
  There is no draft/published state —
  the schema has only is_archived.
  Stated verbatim at
  BatchReviewPage.tsx:22-30.
  Students can read the AI's output
  **before** any human looks at it.
end note

|#F2F2F2|Professor|
:open /professor/upload/batch/[id]/review;

|#DCDCDC|Backend|
:GET /upload/batches/[id]\nscoped by batch_id AND user_id;
:aggregate per lecture:\nslide_count, quiz_count,\nflagged_count;
note right
  flagged = ai_enhanced IS false
  OR needs_review IS true
  → Skip-AI import, synthesis
  failure, vision rescue, or
  empty output.
end note

|#F2F2F2|Professor|
:review cards, one per batch member;
if (card state?) then (still processing)
  :"Still processing" card,\nno editor link;
  stop
elseif (failed) then
  :failure card;
  stop
else (completed)
endif

:open the editor for a lecture;
:toggle "show only flagged";
:correct title / body / summary / MCQs\n(AI assists available in-editor);
:save;

|#DCDCDC|Backend|
:minimal diff patch — only changed fields:\ntitle, content_text, summary, slide_number;
:update or insert quiz_questions\n(unchanged questions skipped);
:**needs_review is never cleared**;
note right
  saveExistingLecture patches only the
  four fields above (lectureService.ts:644-648).
  A corrected slide stays flagged forever, so
  the editor's "auto-reset when the last flagged
  slide is resolved" branch is unreachable
  through editing.
end note

|#F2F2F2|Professor|
:click "Done reviewing";
:written to **localStorage only**\nkey ascend_batch_reviewed_[batchId];
note right
  Non-authoritative: another browser,
  another device, or a cleared cache
  shows the batch as unreviewed again.
  Nothing server-side records that a
  human approved this content.
end note
stop

legend bottom
  For a thesis about turning lecture materials into educational content, the ordering
  here is a first-order finding: the human-in-the-loop is positioned AFTER publication,
  so the review step can correct errors but cannot prevent students seeing them.
endlegend

@enduml
